Added immediate mod-list search by name, author, description, or version.

Separated safe load-order suggestions from [b]Check issues[/b], an on-demand report with exact shared files and compatibility details.

Made warnings and successful-install status more compact, with details available on hover and in the issue report.

Fixed Select all / Deselect all for large mod lists so it no longer repeats expensive checks per mod.

Added read-only validation for legacy cosmetic definitions and stopped reporting their shared category icon as a false file conflict.

Implemented OAuth PKCE for Nexus account access using AIM's public Nexus client registration. No personal Nexus API key or OAuth client secret is included in AIM.

Update checks now surface newer associated Nexus files directly in the mod list. Direct downloads for free accounts may still require the Nexus website's Vortex button, so AIM opens the latest file page when Nexus requires its short-lived website token.

Added recoverable assets.zip state publication and bounded, cancellable Nexus archive extraction. Multi-mod Nexus bundles roll back as a unit; retained backup paths are reported if manual recovery is needed.
